WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.470
... into all white suburbs. By moving&nbsp;
North and by concerning itself with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:09.090
equality in housing and employment,&nbsp;
the Civil Rights Movement began to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:13.080
encounter increased resistance,&nbsp;
the so-called white backlash.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:29.422
During these marches, King and other demonstrators&nbsp;
were struck by bricks and bottles. "Oh I've been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.422 --> 00:00:41.860
hit so many times, I'm immune to it." "How&nbsp;
do you feel about this reception?" "Well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:48.010
this is a terrible thing, I've been in many&nbsp;
demonstrations all across the South but I can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:55.930
say that I have never seen even in Mississippi&nbsp;
and Alabama mobs as hostile and as hate-filled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.930 --> 00:00:59.830
as I've seen in Chicago." "But the march&nbsp;
will go on anyway?" "Oh very definitely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:10.012
we can't stop the march, we'll be going on&nbsp;
in a few minutes." "Do you feel you are in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.012 --> 00:01:10.550
closed society, Dr. King, here in the southwest&nbsp;
side of Chicago?" "Oh yes, this is definitely a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:11.440
closed society, but we're gonna make it an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:18.190
open society and we feel that we have to do&nbsp;
it this way to bring the evil out into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:23.680
open so that this community will be forced&nbsp;
to deal with it." "And so the backlash.."

